## 3. Step-by-Step Configuration

### 3.1 Layer 2 Configuration on Switch1

Creation of the VLANs, assignment of access ports, and setup of the 802.1Q trunk:

```text
Switch1> enable
Switch1# configure terminal

! 1. Create the network VLANs
Switch1(config)# vlan 10
Switch1(config-vlan)# name ADMIN
Switch1(config-vlan)# vlan 20
Switch1(config-vlan)# name Production
Switch1(config-vlan)# vlan 99
Switch1(config-vlan)# name NATIVE_VLAN
Switch1(config-vlan)# exit

! 2. Configure access ports for the hosts
Switch1(config)# interface fa0/24
Switch1(config-if)# switchport mode access
Switch1(config-if)# switchport access vlan 10
Switch1(config-if)# spanning-tree portfast

Switch1(config)# interface fa0/23
Switch1(config-if)# switchport mode access
Switch1(config-if)# switchport access vlan 20
Switch1(config-if)# spanning-tree portfast

! 3. Configure the 802.1Q trunk toward the router
Switch1(config)# interface gig0/1
Switch1(config-if)# switchport mode trunk
Switch1(config-if)# switchport trunk native vlan 99
Switch1(config-if)# switchport trunk allowed vlan 10,20,99
Switch1(config-if)# exit
```

### 3.2 Layer 3 and DHCP Configuration on Router1

Enabling the physical interface, creating the 802.1Q subinterfaces, and defining the dynamic IP address pools:

```text
Router1> enable
Router1# configure terminal

! 1. Bring up the main physical interface (no direct IP address)
Router1(config)# interface gigabitethernet 0/0
Router1(config-if)# no ip address
Router1(config-if)# no shutdown
Router1(config-if)# exit

! 2. Configure ROAS subinterfaces
Router1(config)# interface gigabitethernet 0/0.10
Router1(config-subif)# encapsulation dot1Q 10
Router1(config-subif)# ip address 192.168.10.1 255.255.255.0

Router1(config)# interface gigabitethernet 0/0.20
Router1(config-subif)# encapsulation dot1Q 20
Router1(config-subif)# ip address 192.168.20.1 255.255.255.0
Router1(config-subif)# exit

! 3. Exclude gateways to prevent IP conflicts
Router1(config)# ip dhcp excluded-address 192.168.10.1
Router1(config)# ip dhcp excluded-address 192.168.20.1

! 4. Define DHCP pools
Router1(config)# ip dhcp pool VLAN10
Router1(dhcp-config)# network 192.168.10.0 255.255.255.0
Router1(dhcp-config)# default-router 192.168.10.1
Router1(dhcp-config)# dns-server 8.8.8.8

Router1(config)# ip dhcp pool VLAN20
Router1(dhcp-config)# network 192.168.20.0 255.255.255.0
Router1(dhcp-config)# default-router 192.168.20.1
Router1(dhcp-config)# dns-server 8.8.8.8
```

